{"term":"kick","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:3414b24701474f76d3","definition":"To strike or hit with the foot or other extremity of the leg.","example":"Did you kick your brother?","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kick#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a8f1b901d7d21d5c1a","definition":"To make a sharp jerking movement of the leg, as to strike something.","example":"He enjoyed the simple pleasure of watching the kickline kick.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kick#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:eb448176c0b2f2a4bd","definition":"To direct to a particular place by a blow with the foot or leg.","example":"Kick the ball into the goal.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kick#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c048107c0580e7af64","definition":"To eject summarily.","example":"\"He's been mad at me ever since I fired him off'n my payroll. After I kicked him off'n my ranch he run for sheriff, and the night of the election everybody was so drunk they voted for him by mistake, or for a joke, or somethin', and since he's been in office he's been lettin' the sheepmen steal me right out of house and home.\"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl"